# Every element inside its own parent, at both sizes. Part 2 of 4.
#
# assert_no_overflow asks whether an element is on screen, which a row
# overflowing a panel mid-screen passes. This asks the question the name does.
#
# Both sizes on purpose: nearly everything found here held at exactly 720p and
# came apart above it, usually a fixed-pixel box whose padding scales with the
# screen until the padding is larger than the box.
#
# Split four ways because 91 screens in one script runs past the 30s timeout.
# composer_lab is left out: its third field is a deliberate "wrapping is off on
# this one" demo, so the overflow there is the point.

goto_screen deadspace_settings
wait 0.3
resize 1280 720
wait 0.2
assert_within_parents
resize 1920 1080
wait 0.2
assert_within_parents

